WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.360
As with every Tarantino film, Once Upon a
Time in Hollywood is rich with storytelling

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.400
depth and meaning, especially as the film
reaches its climax.

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:13.080
Now that the movie's out, it's time to dig
deep into the ending.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.730
Let's get the biggest development of the ending
out of the way: Once Upon a Time in Hollywood

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:23.620
is a movie in which the Manson family murders
didn't happen the way they did in real life.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.180
It's clear from Cliff's visit to the Spahn
Movie Ranch that Charles Manson's commune

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:33.019
is up to something devious, but when it comes
time to commit the infamous murders on Cielo

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:37.700
Drive on the night of August 8th, historical
fact gives way to fiction.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.960
One drug-fueled decision to change plans and
try to murder Rick Dalton creates a ripple

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:43.460
effect.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:48.900
Sharon Tate and her friends survive that night,
and three key members of Manson's family do

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:49.400
not.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.700
Though the film ends before it can explore
the full extent of this ripple effect, it's

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:59.469
safe to assume that the black cloud created
by the Manson murders in 1969 was changed

00:00:59.469 --> 00:01:01.040
in a number of key ways.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:07.200
Joan Didion famously wrote that the night
Sharon Tate died was the night the 1960s ended.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:12.159
The decade was about to end anyway, but perhaps
Rick and Cliff's acts of self-defense were

00:01:12.159 --> 00:01:17.079
enough to keep the feeling of the 1960s alive
in Hollywood for at least a little longer.

00:01:18.079 --> 00:01:23.270
The last shot of Once Upon a Time in Hollywood
shows us Rick, having torched Susan Atkins

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:27.770
in his pool during the attack on his house,
being invited up to Sharon Tate's home for

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:28.400
drinks.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:33.060
It's the realization of a fantasy Rick has
been nurturing ever since he figured out that

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:38.420
the hottest director in town, Roman Polanski,
and his rising star wife were his neighbors.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.820
To Rick, they're the people who can get him
into all the best Hollywood circles, the people

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:45.060
who can resurrect his struggling career.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.970
The film offers us no promises as to what
lies in store for Rick's professional life

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:54.619
going forward, but within minutes of meeting
Jay Sebring, he's already bragging about the

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:55.760
night's events.

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:00.389
At worst, he's going to become a hit at various
Hollywood parties for a while.

00:02:00.389 --> 00:02:05.009
At best, Rick could end up with everything
from a role in Polanski's next film to a brand

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:06.260
new TV series.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:12.100
Even though Rick gets to brag about the events,
Cliff takes the brunt of the Manson Family's

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:16.320
attack, which includes some bumps, bruises,
and a knife embedded in his hip.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:21.080
Still, he's cheerful as the ambulance takes
him away, promising Rick that he'll live to

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.380
fight another day.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.060
Once Upon a Time in Hollywood establishes
early on that Cliff's reputation is in the

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:30.760
gutter since he likely had a hand in his wife's
suspicious death.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.980
It's hard to believe everyone would forget
about that because he fought off attackers

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.040
at Rick's house.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:40.780
If anything, it will likely add to his reputation
as a violent man in some circles.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:46.110
However, in other circles, it could also speak
to his reputation as a badass with a long

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:47.460
career in stunt work.

00:02:47.989 --> 00:02:52.879
Maybe retellings of the event will help make
people like Randy more open to Cliff's whole

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:53.400
"vibe."

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.160
"I don't dig him.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.820
And I don't dig the vibe he brings to the
set."

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:06.019
The bedrock of Once Upon a Time in Hollywood
is ultimately the friendship between Cliff

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:11.680
and Rick, something which ends up transcending
any dynamic as simple as leading man and stunt

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:12.180
double.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:17.620
These men are in some ways closer than brothers,
and that relationship is the throughline that

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:18.560
carries the film.

00:03:19.189 --> 00:03:23.520
In the final minutes of the film, it's very
clear that Rick feels indebted to Cliff for

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:24.500
saving his life.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:29.840
No matter what happens from this point on,
Cliff and Rick are stronger and closer than

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:30.340
ever.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:35.560
At the time of her death, Sharon Tate's acting
career consisted of only a handful of film

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:41.060
roles and a few stints on TV, most notably
a recurring role on The Beverly Hillbillies.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.879
Still, as Once Upon A Time In…

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:46.520
Hollywood shows, she was a talented actor
with a bright future.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:51.000
It's impossible to guess what Sharon Tate's
full professional future would hold in a world

00:03:51.019 --> 00:03:55.640
in which she's still alive, Once Upon A Time
seems to hint that the best is still to come

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:56.280
for Tate.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:01.400
It's this bittersweet notion, a world in which
Tate is allowed to live on, that most sticks

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.920
with you as you leave the theater.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.540
Because of the mythology that's sprung up
around her in death, the potential life she

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:09.900
never got to have carries even more weight.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:15.340
Even before the Manson family begins its attack
at the end of the film, there are plenty of

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:19.920
key differences that establish the alternate
universe in which the film takes place.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:24.680
The biggest difference is obviously that the
Tate murders never take place, but the historical

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:29.140
discrepancies throughout the film establish
that the world is changed even before that

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:30.140
crime is avoided.

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:35.410
What else changes in this new timeline Tarantino
has established, one in which Tate doesn't

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:38.320
die and Polanski doesn't come home to a crime
scene?

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:42.900
What does Joan Didion write about if not the
Manson murders and subsequent trial?

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:47.620
Does Bruce Lee, whose legend also looms large
in the film, somehow also get to survive his

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.140
own tragic early death just four years later?

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:54.620
Do the Beatles ever learn about Manson's strange
interpretation of their lyrics?

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:58.160
"Uh, I don't know.”

